1
00:00:52,511 --> 00:00:53,387
ALL PERSONS, LOCATIONS, RELIGIONS,
INCIDENTS, AND ORGANIZATIONS IN THIS DRAMA

2
00:00:53,512 --> 00:00:54,346
ARE FICTITIOUS

3
00:00:54,472 --> 00:00:55,306
CHILD ACTORS HAVE FILMED SAFELY
UNDER PARENTAL SUPERVISION

4
00:00:55,431 --> 00:00:56,265
SCENES INVOLVING ANIMALS WERE FILMED
SAFELY WITH EXPERT ADVICE AND COOPERATION

5
00:00:59,769 --> 00:01:00,895
Mom, it's spicy!

6
00:01:01,020 --> 00:01:02,980
-Here, have some water.
-Water.

7
00:01:03,105 --> 00:01:04,064
Here you go.

8
00:01:05,566 --> 00:01:07,693
I'll finish eating in a minute
and watch Wan-do.

9
00:01:07,818 --> 00:01:10,696
It's fine. You'll get indigestion.
Take your time.

10
00:01:10,821 --> 00:01:12,656
Oh, no.

11
00:01:12,782 --> 00:01:14,366
When did you spill this?

12
00:01:14,492 --> 00:01:16,744
I just bought you these clothes.

13
00:01:19,705 --> 00:01:20,790
Eat up.

14
00:01:22,374 --> 00:01:24,210
Sweetie, are you not going to eat?

15
00:01:25,211 --> 00:01:27,922
Want me to rinse the kimchi? Is it spicy?

16
00:01:28,589 --> 00:01:32,468
Dad, tell her I'm not a baby
who can't eat kimchi.

17
00:01:35,596 --> 00:01:39,058
Lee Mi-do, how long
are you going to be like this?

18
00:01:39,183 --> 00:01:41,143
It's been two weeks.

19
00:01:41,268 --> 00:01:44,063
Look, if you're mad at me,
just tell me straight.

20
00:01:45,147 --> 00:01:46,106
I'll talk to her.

21
00:01:46,232 --> 00:01:47,525
Jeez, this girl.

22
00:01:49,527 --> 00:01:51,362
What's wrong with my princess?

23
00:01:51,487 --> 00:01:54,114
I'm sad when you're like this
on a family trip.

24
00:01:55,157 --> 00:01:57,368
What is it? Is it because of piano class?

25
00:01:59,203 --> 00:02:02,206
I'll start saving up my extra pay
this month, okay?

26
00:02:03,207 --> 00:02:04,124
It's not that?

27
00:02:04,250 --> 00:02:07,086
Then what? Art class? Ballet?

28
00:02:07,878 --> 00:02:10,673
Oh! I want to do taekwondo.

29
00:02:10,798 --> 00:02:12,174
-Taekwondo?
-Yes.

30
00:02:12,299 --> 00:02:13,217
Got it.

31
00:02:13,968 --> 00:02:15,469
-I want a fire truck.
-Then…

32
00:02:15,594 --> 00:02:16,804
-You too?
-A fire truck?

33
00:02:16,929 --> 00:02:19,348
I want something too.
Please buy me a lipstick.

34
00:02:19,473 --> 00:02:20,724
-Lipstick?
-Yes.

35
00:02:21,267 --> 00:02:23,185
-A lipstick for Suk-hui!
-Yes!

36
00:02:24,103 --> 00:02:27,523
My life's been totally messed up
since I met your mom.

37
00:02:34,321 --> 00:02:39,285
After everything I've done for her?

38
00:02:40,953 --> 00:02:44,540
I even raised her brat
who isn't even my own blood.

39
00:02:45,124 --> 00:02:46,000
Jeez.

40
00:02:49,879 --> 00:02:50,880
What?

41
00:02:52,006 --> 00:02:53,924
Are you pissed
that I'm insulting your mom?

42
00:02:54,049 --> 00:02:58,304
My mom and the hardware store guy
have nothing going on.

43
00:02:58,429 --> 00:02:59,805
Oh, really?

44
00:02:59,930 --> 00:03:02,558
He only came to our house today

45
00:03:02,683 --> 00:03:06,145
because the light was broken.
He came to fix it.

46
00:03:09,523 --> 00:03:10,691
You know it too, right?

47
00:03:11,734 --> 00:03:14,778
That your mom isn't coming back for you.

48
00:03:20,117 --> 00:03:22,786
Well, we're in the same boat.

49
00:03:25,331 --> 00:03:26,248
All right, let's go.

50
00:03:26,373 --> 00:03:27,499
-Okay.
-I'm first!

51
00:03:27,625 --> 00:03:28,792
Slow down.

52
00:03:33,213 --> 00:03:34,965
Oh my gosh! Are you okay?

53
00:03:35,090 --> 00:03:37,176
-Mi-do!
-Oh, I'm sorry.

54
00:03:37,301 --> 00:03:38,302
Are you okay?

55
00:03:41,513 --> 00:03:42,681
Oh, no. Does it burn?

56
00:03:42,806 --> 00:03:45,184
Oh my gosh, he must be scared.

57
00:03:46,727 --> 00:03:48,687
Again, I'm so incredibly sorry.

58
00:03:48,812 --> 00:03:50,689
Oh, it's fine.

59
00:03:51,398 --> 00:03:53,317
You should really take him to a doctor.

60
00:03:53,442 --> 00:03:54,902
I'll take care of it.

61
00:03:55,027 --> 00:03:56,654
Should we come with you?

62
00:03:56,779 --> 00:03:58,697
-She looks like Kim Hee-seon.
-It's fine.

63
00:03:58,822 --> 00:04:00,699
-Your mom.
-I'll take him to the doctor.

64
00:04:01,367 --> 00:04:03,160
-You really should.
-Do you like dinosaurs?

65
00:04:03,285 --> 00:04:05,371
I'll take care of that myself.

66
00:04:05,496 --> 00:04:08,415
You probably fell for it
because my mom did that for you,

67
00:04:08,540 --> 00:04:09,750
but it's all fake.

68
00:04:10,501 --> 00:04:12,127
My mom is stronger than a dinosaur.

69
00:04:12,252 --> 00:04:14,672
Ever been hit in the back of the head
with a handbag?

70
00:04:15,255 --> 00:04:16,131
It really hurts.

71
00:04:17,049 --> 00:04:18,342
That doesn't hurt.

72
00:04:19,510 --> 00:04:21,053
You promised me, man to man.

73
00:04:21,720 --> 00:04:23,973
Take him to a doctor and call me.

74
00:04:24,098 --> 00:04:25,683
I've memorized your pager number.

75
00:04:25,808 --> 00:04:28,936
Jeez, you have trust issues.

76
00:04:30,437 --> 00:04:31,271
Hey.

77
00:04:33,899 --> 00:04:34,817
Sweetie.

78
00:04:36,068 --> 00:04:38,696
You must've been so scared. I'm so sorry.

79
00:04:42,700 --> 00:04:43,951
Go see a doctor.

80
00:04:44,702 --> 00:04:46,704
Okay? Promise me.

81
00:04:48,580 --> 00:04:50,499
What are you doing? Let's go.

82
00:04:58,048 --> 00:04:58,882
Hey!

83
00:05:03,804 --> 00:05:05,264
Since you seem to like dinosaurs.

84
00:05:15,482 --> 00:05:17,401
Let's just go already.

85
00:05:24,700 --> 00:05:26,660
NO SWIMMING

86
00:05:26,785 --> 00:05:28,537
I hope he saw a doctor.

87
00:05:30,122 --> 00:05:32,416
We really should've gone with them.

88
00:05:34,251 --> 00:05:36,003
I got his pager number.

89
00:05:37,087 --> 00:05:39,715
Plus, he said he knows
the restaurant owner, so…

90
00:05:40,507 --> 00:05:42,301
if he doesn't call by tonight, we'll ask.

91
00:05:43,385 --> 00:05:44,386
Okay.

92
00:05:48,182 --> 00:05:51,101
Then again,
I have my own things to worry about.

93
00:05:53,979 --> 00:05:55,647
What is it, really?

94
00:05:56,899 --> 00:05:58,358
Is this about the cotton candy?

95
00:05:58,484 --> 00:05:59,860
I told you to have some.

96
00:06:00,611 --> 00:06:02,905
I didn't just buy it for your brother.

97
00:06:03,030 --> 00:06:07,618
Dad, can you tell her I hate cotton candy
because it rots your teeth?

98
00:06:11,080 --> 00:06:14,249
Honey, could you ask her
why she's sulking so much,

99
00:06:14,374 --> 00:06:17,169
and tell her she's acting
like a total baby right now?

100
00:06:17,294 --> 00:06:19,463
Jeez, why are you doing this, too?

101
00:06:22,091 --> 00:06:24,593
Can my princess whisper it just to me?

102
00:06:25,302 --> 00:06:26,678
What made you so upset?

103
00:06:28,013 --> 00:06:29,389
Oh, just leave her alone.

104
00:06:29,515 --> 00:06:32,643
You keep doing that,
you're just spoiling her.

105
00:06:32,768 --> 00:06:36,146
She never listens
and always causes trouble.

106
00:06:36,271 --> 00:06:37,356
That's it.

107
00:06:37,481 --> 00:06:40,025
I should just abandon her
at some random house.

108
00:06:40,150 --> 00:06:42,444
When you get old,
I'm going to abandon you!

109
00:06:43,195 --> 00:06:45,322
I'll leave you deep in the mountains!

110
00:06:57,960 --> 00:06:59,086
What did you just say?

111
00:07:00,879 --> 00:07:01,922
Lee Mi-do.

112
00:07:03,048 --> 00:07:04,758
I learned it in history class.

113
00:07:05,384 --> 00:07:07,886
It's called  goryeojang .
When parents got old,

114
00:07:08,011 --> 00:07:09,513
they were left in the woods.

115
00:07:10,180 --> 00:07:12,015
My teacher taught me that.

116
00:07:12,141 --> 00:07:15,519
No, that's wrong.
Your teacher must've said it's bad

117
00:07:16,228 --> 00:07:17,604
and you should never do it.

118
00:07:17,729 --> 00:07:20,524
You really hurt Mom's feelings just now.

119
00:07:20,649 --> 00:07:22,568
You said a really mean thing to her.

120
00:07:22,693 --> 00:07:25,445
But Mom hurt my feelings even more!

121
00:07:25,988 --> 00:07:29,241
She forgets every single thing I tell her!

122
00:07:29,950 --> 00:07:33,954
She forgot I wanted to wear
my rabbit fur vest on Friday.

123
00:07:34,496 --> 00:07:37,166
She forgot that I'm good
at eating spicy food.

124
00:07:37,916 --> 00:07:40,794
She forgot I wanted to eat the pink ham.

125
00:07:40,919 --> 00:07:42,004
And…

126
00:07:42,546 --> 00:07:45,090
she forgot I like silkworm pupae,
not cotton candy!

127
00:07:45,215 --> 00:07:46,800
She forgot everything!

128
00:07:51,680 --> 00:07:52,514
There, there.

129
00:07:53,891 --> 00:07:54,892
My sweet Mi-do.

130
00:07:55,017 --> 00:07:57,728
You must've been so upset, right?

131
00:08:00,189 --> 00:08:01,273
But Mi-do…

132
00:08:02,441 --> 00:08:05,527
Mom doesn't just forget what you tell her.

133
00:08:05,652 --> 00:08:07,988
She always forgets what I say, too.

134
00:08:08,697 --> 00:08:11,366
You saw me wearing
mismatched socks the other day.

135
00:08:13,160 --> 00:08:14,912
You only have one mom,

136
00:08:15,746 --> 00:08:17,289
but Mom has three kids.

137
00:08:17,414 --> 00:08:19,583
Wait, four, including me.

138
00:08:21,627 --> 00:08:22,502
Mi-do.

139
00:08:23,545 --> 00:08:25,255
If you don't speak up,

140
00:08:25,380 --> 00:08:26,924
if you don't tell us,

141
00:08:27,049 --> 00:08:29,801
even though Mom and I love you so much,

142
00:08:29,927 --> 00:08:31,637
we can't read your mind.

143
00:08:32,554 --> 00:08:35,265
It's not because we love you any less.

144
00:08:36,183 --> 00:08:39,144
We don't know because you don't tell us.

145
00:08:41,313 --> 00:08:44,399
I want you to be someone who can be honest

146
00:08:44,942 --> 00:08:48,862
about your feelings
with the people you love.

147
00:08:51,114 --> 00:08:51,949
Can you?

148
00:08:54,493 --> 00:08:55,452
Okay, promise me.

149
00:09:06,213 --> 00:09:08,882
-Someone fell in the water!
-Someone fell in the water!

150
00:09:09,007 --> 00:09:10,717
Hurry, help!

151
00:09:33,240 --> 00:09:34,283
Honey.

152
00:09:38,829 --> 00:09:40,872
Oh my God. Honey, wake up.

153
00:09:41,957 --> 00:09:44,293
Wake up!

154
00:09:44,418 --> 00:09:46,128
Wake up!

155
00:09:53,844 --> 00:09:56,930
No, no!

156
00:10:01,685 --> 00:10:02,853
Honey.

157
00:10:15,866 --> 00:10:16,742
Honey.

158
00:10:31,715 --> 00:10:37,596
10. WHAT DO OUR SCARS LOOK LIKE?

159
00:10:37,721 --> 00:10:38,972
ESTIMATE

160
00:10:41,683 --> 00:10:43,852
I'm rejecting this estimate.

161
00:10:45,520 --> 00:10:47,773
You need to give me a reason.

162
00:10:47,898 --> 00:10:50,609
We clearly followed the guidelines.
What's the problem?

163
00:10:50,734 --> 00:10:53,153
Is 600 million won
really a feasible amount?

164
00:10:56,406 --> 00:10:58,200
The purchase cost listed here

165
00:10:58,992 --> 00:11:01,078
was calculated to reflect
the market price decline

166
00:11:01,203 --> 00:11:03,330
resulting from increased
raw material procurement.

167
00:11:03,455 --> 00:11:07,376
But you completely left out the burden
of rising fuel costs on logistics.

168
00:11:09,336 --> 00:11:11,797
Surcharges were added
due to Middle East oil price risks.

169
00:11:11,922 --> 00:11:13,507
You can't submit estimates like this.

170
00:11:14,383 --> 00:11:17,844
If it was a mistake, it's incompetence.
If it was intentional, it's deception.

171
00:11:18,887 --> 00:11:20,639
I can't just keep this on my end.

172
00:11:20,764 --> 00:11:22,849
It needs to be reported to the audit team.

173
00:11:22,974 --> 00:11:25,644
Submitting a false estimate
is grounds for disciplinary action.

174
00:11:25,769 --> 00:11:28,647
Resubmit it in three days
using the last three months' statistics.

175
00:11:28,772 --> 00:11:30,690
I'll withhold final approval until then.

176
00:11:37,072 --> 00:11:40,492
Who is it? Who leaked our plan?

177
00:11:46,373 --> 00:11:47,624
Look me in the eye.

178
00:11:47,749 --> 00:11:49,042
Within the last week,

179
00:11:49,167 --> 00:11:51,044
did you drink with Namgung Ho?

180
00:11:51,920 --> 00:11:52,754
I did.

181
00:11:52,879 --> 00:11:54,923
Did Namgung Ho pay for the drinks?

182
00:11:55,048 --> 00:11:55,966
He did.

183
00:11:56,633 --> 00:11:58,552
But I don't think I said anything.

184
00:11:58,677 --> 00:12:00,011
Why are you smiling?

185
00:12:00,137 --> 00:12:01,638
Did you get drunk that day?

186
00:12:02,347 --> 00:12:03,432
I did.

187
00:12:04,850 --> 00:12:06,226
But I…

188
00:12:07,561 --> 00:12:10,021
You…

189
00:12:10,147 --> 00:12:11,690
You committed drunken treason.

190
00:12:11,815 --> 00:12:12,899
You drunk-sabotaged us!

191
00:12:14,067 --> 00:12:15,902
You told that snake Namgung Ho everything!

192
00:12:18,196 --> 00:12:20,240
But was it really me?

193
00:12:20,365 --> 00:12:21,491
I don't think so.

194
00:12:21,616 --> 00:12:22,492
If not you,

195
00:12:23,076 --> 00:12:25,162
do you think Ms. Park did it?

196
00:12:25,287 --> 00:12:26,496
She got top evaluations

197
00:12:26,621 --> 00:12:28,373
and last year's best employee award.

198
00:12:28,498 --> 00:12:30,083
She's not stupid like you

199
00:12:30,208 --> 00:12:31,585
to sabotage us while drunk!

200
00:12:31,710 --> 00:12:32,878
I think I did.

201
00:12:33,003 --> 00:12:34,880
Hear that? She said you did it!

202
00:12:36,631 --> 00:12:37,674
Wait, what?

203
00:12:37,799 --> 00:12:39,843
I wasn't drunk

204
00:12:40,594 --> 00:12:42,220
or stupid.

205
00:12:44,848 --> 00:12:46,224
It was a honey trap.

206
00:12:48,268 --> 00:12:50,187
How did TF Team 3's cost adjustment go?

207
00:12:50,312 --> 00:12:54,858
Imported raw material prices vary
based on local supply, right?

208
00:12:55,400 --> 00:12:59,362
He pulled off a bit of a bluff
using the increased crop volume.

209
00:13:01,990 --> 00:13:03,200
That's a relief.

210
00:13:06,786 --> 00:13:08,079
It was a honey trap.

211
00:13:10,916 --> 00:13:12,501
He tricked me.

212
00:13:16,922 --> 00:13:18,632
You were holding my hand

213
00:13:18,757 --> 00:13:20,550
just to get info out of me, right?

214
00:13:20,675 --> 00:13:23,303
-It was a honey trap.
-Did you join the company because of me?

215
00:13:23,428 --> 00:13:27,015
Procurement's initial 600-million-won
offer was ridiculous anyway.

216
00:13:27,849 --> 00:13:30,101
Did you date Sun-cheol
while having feelings for me?

217
00:13:31,520 --> 00:13:33,730
I heard you and Manager Jeong
are close now.

218
00:13:33,855 --> 00:13:34,940
What happened there?

219
00:13:35,649 --> 00:13:37,442
How's Sun-cheol doing lately?

220
00:13:41,988 --> 00:13:44,991
I know you're dodging the question
by embarrassing me.

221
00:13:45,116 --> 00:13:46,952
Give me a straight answer.

222
00:13:48,828 --> 00:13:50,288
I just followed the rules.

223
00:13:51,581 --> 00:13:54,251
Procurement can't approve
false invoices, can they?

224
00:13:55,126 --> 00:13:56,127
Any issues with that?

225
00:13:58,547 --> 00:14:00,215
No, none.

226
00:14:05,220 --> 00:14:06,346
Let's make eye contact.

227
00:14:08,515 --> 00:14:10,058
Can you last four seconds this time?

228
00:14:10,183 --> 00:14:11,810
If I last ten seconds,

229
00:14:12,561 --> 00:14:14,145
you must grant me one wish.

230
00:14:17,816 --> 00:14:18,817
Deal.

231
00:14:35,625 --> 00:14:36,668
Another honey trap!

232
00:14:38,712 --> 00:14:41,590
-That's a foul.
-How is it a foul when there are no rules?

233
00:14:45,093 --> 00:14:46,761
Keep your promise.

234
00:14:46,886 --> 00:14:48,221
If I last ten seconds--

235
00:14:48,346 --> 00:14:51,016
I'm never telling you
what you want to know.

236
00:14:52,100 --> 00:14:53,310
Don't expect it.

237
00:14:53,435 --> 00:14:55,770
I can find that out on my own.

238
00:14:55,895 --> 00:14:57,147
I'm capable enough.

239
00:15:00,066 --> 00:15:01,651
If I last ten seconds,

240
00:15:03,695 --> 00:15:06,865
tell me a secret of yours
that Ms. Lee doesn't know.

241
00:15:15,290 --> 00:15:16,166
Okay.

242
00:15:17,208 --> 00:15:18,043
You better.

243
00:15:22,797 --> 00:15:25,175
I'm really going to do it. I swear I will.

244
00:15:25,300 --> 00:15:26,384
No more honey traps.

245
00:15:45,987 --> 00:15:46,863
No.

246
00:15:47,530 --> 00:15:48,865
You let me go.

247
00:15:49,407 --> 00:15:52,494
And back then, I loved you so much.

248
00:15:53,203 --> 00:15:55,038
Hey, Mun-yeong!

249
00:15:55,163 --> 00:15:56,748
Mun-yeong, what are you doing?

250
00:15:56,873 --> 00:15:59,793
I messed up, okay?
I won't survive if you go.

251
00:15:59,918 --> 00:16:00,794
Mun-yeong.

252
00:16:01,503 --> 00:16:03,171
I said I'm sorry!

253
00:16:03,296 --> 00:16:04,547
Mun-yeong!

254
00:16:05,298 --> 00:16:06,383
Mun-yeong!

255
00:16:07,008 --> 00:16:08,718
Even if you hate me, please.

256
00:16:10,011 --> 00:16:12,222
I'm so sorry, Mun-yeong!

257
00:16:13,807 --> 00:16:16,476
I can't live without you, Mun-yeong!

258
00:16:16,601 --> 00:16:17,435
Mun-yeong!

259
00:16:17,560 --> 00:16:20,689
SEOUL FAMILY COURT
SEOUL ADMINISTRATIVE COURT

260
00:16:20,814 --> 00:16:22,190
Please reconsider.

261
00:16:22,315 --> 00:16:24,192
Just one last time.

262
00:16:24,317 --> 00:16:26,152
Just once, please?

263
00:16:26,820 --> 00:16:27,987
Why on earth

264
00:16:29,197 --> 00:16:32,158
do we have to split up?

265
00:16:32,992 --> 00:16:34,661
Please, I'm begging you.

266
00:16:35,328 --> 00:16:36,705
Please…

267
00:17:07,193 --> 00:17:08,027
KO MUN-YEONG LAB

268
00:17:10,238 --> 00:17:11,948
I just can't understand…

269
00:17:36,181 --> 00:17:38,892
I can't do this anymore. I can't go on.

270
00:17:41,728 --> 00:17:43,605
You used to run a kilometer
in three minutes.

271
00:17:43,730 --> 00:17:45,732
-Just run.
-Wait!

272
00:17:45,857 --> 00:17:47,400
I'm in my thirties now, okay?

273
00:17:47,525 --> 00:17:48,610
And lately,

274
00:17:48,735 --> 00:17:50,570
Do-Re-Mi-Fa-Sol is driving me nuts.

275
00:17:51,321 --> 00:17:53,656
Also, Mi-do's been MIA for three days.

276
00:17:55,074 --> 00:17:57,160
Man, at times like this,

277
00:17:57,285 --> 00:17:59,245
I guess I'm just like her.

278
00:18:00,914 --> 00:18:02,165
I'm sad.

279
00:18:04,626 --> 00:18:05,877
MIA for three days?

280
00:18:06,544 --> 00:18:08,546
Yes, she said it's a stomach bug.

281
00:18:08,671 --> 00:18:11,216
You know her routine
when she goes off the grid.

282
00:18:11,341 --> 00:18:13,426
Her phone is on, and she answers,

283
00:18:14,052 --> 00:18:15,512
but she won't show her face.

284
00:18:16,846 --> 00:18:17,680
What?

285
00:18:19,974 --> 00:18:20,809
You didn't know?

286
00:18:22,227 --> 00:18:23,353
It's been four days.

287
00:18:23,478 --> 00:18:24,896
Pay attention to her, man.

288
00:18:25,605 --> 00:18:26,564
No, it's been three…

289
00:18:30,193 --> 00:18:31,277
Wait, is it four?

290
00:18:31,820 --> 00:18:32,654
Hey, wait!

291
00:18:37,408 --> 00:18:40,203
TIN CAN BASTARD

292
00:18:48,795 --> 00:18:49,963
TIN CAN BASTARD

293
00:18:50,129 --> 00:18:52,006
MISSED CALL
TIN CAN BASTARD

294
00:18:56,386 --> 00:18:59,889
How can you love the man
who caused your father's death?

295
00:19:11,442 --> 00:19:12,735
Unbelievable.

296
00:19:12,861 --> 00:19:15,572
She said she goes to work every weekday.
Where is she?

297
00:19:17,907 --> 00:19:19,742
Is her phone just for show?

298
00:19:20,493 --> 00:19:21,828
Jeez.

299
00:19:23,162 --> 00:19:24,205
Huh?

300
00:19:25,248 --> 00:19:27,333
He's your junior from the army, right?

301
00:19:30,920 --> 00:19:33,882
The lawyer who got into
a car accident with Mi-do.

302
00:19:36,384 --> 00:19:37,844
-Well, that was--
-Gwan-u, you punk.

303
00:19:39,345 --> 00:19:41,097
I told you never to come back.

304
00:19:47,937 --> 00:19:50,356
He lost his house
and property trading crypto,

305
00:19:50,481 --> 00:19:52,150
and he keeps coming to me for money.

306
00:19:52,275 --> 00:19:53,526
I'm going nuts.

307
00:19:57,780 --> 00:19:58,698
Oh.

308
00:20:13,922 --> 00:20:15,131
Hey.

309
00:20:20,303 --> 00:20:21,387
Sir, yes, sir!

310
00:20:23,348 --> 00:20:25,767
I lost everything trading crypto,

311
00:20:26,392 --> 00:20:28,353
but I can still afford this, sir.

312
00:20:28,478 --> 00:20:30,021
No Eggs Royale, my baby's favorite?

313
00:20:31,356 --> 00:20:35,276
My baby loves avocado
on a smoked salmon Benedict.

314
00:20:35,401 --> 00:20:36,235
Remember that.

315
00:20:49,916 --> 00:20:52,835
I'm from Daeho Unit, Class 1035,
and you're from Class 1047.

316
00:20:53,586 --> 00:20:56,172
When you were a private,
your superior, Corporal Park,

317
00:20:56,297 --> 00:20:58,299
was beating the crap out of you
in the bathroom.

318
00:20:58,424 --> 00:21:00,093
I stepped in and saved you.

319
00:21:00,218 --> 00:21:03,137
After that, you followed me
whenever I went to the PX store.

320
00:21:04,347 --> 00:21:06,516
By the way, your nickname, Gwan-u,

321
00:21:06,641 --> 00:21:08,977
means "crybaby loser who needs attention."

322
00:21:11,646 --> 00:21:14,357
Our youngest will be done washing up
in about five minutes.

323
00:21:15,358 --> 00:21:16,859
Memorize it perfectly.

324
00:21:17,610 --> 00:21:19,779
You think you're really their father?

325
00:21:23,783 --> 00:21:24,742
What?

326
00:21:25,785 --> 00:21:28,663
Trying to fill the void
of the father you killed?

327
00:21:29,789 --> 00:21:31,457
Don't do that to Mi-do.

328
00:21:33,292 --> 00:21:35,253
Don't take cheap shots like that

329
00:21:36,546 --> 00:21:37,505
at Mi-do.

330
00:21:42,969 --> 00:21:44,345
I guess you already did.

331
00:21:48,725 --> 00:21:50,143
Oh.

332
00:21:51,310 --> 00:21:54,981
So, it was you who made Mi-do disappear.

333
00:22:03,406 --> 00:22:04,574
Gwan-u.

334
00:22:06,117 --> 00:22:08,286
If you hurt Mi-do any further,

335
00:22:09,829 --> 00:22:11,122
you're a dead man.

336
00:22:13,166 --> 00:22:15,126
I will actually kill you.

337
00:22:22,050 --> 00:22:23,760
Daeho Unit, Class 1047.

338
00:22:24,427 --> 00:22:26,345
From March to November 2013.

339
00:22:26,471 --> 00:22:28,389
By the way, Daeho Unit is in Changwon.

340
00:22:31,309 --> 00:22:34,062
He's sharper than he looks. Don't mess up.

341
00:22:39,817 --> 00:22:41,944
You didn't lend him money, did you?

342
00:22:43,362 --> 00:22:45,198
I think he's in a pyramid scheme.

343
00:22:45,323 --> 00:22:46,282
Be careful.

344
00:22:48,117 --> 00:22:50,036
Look at his eyes. He's lost it.

345
00:22:51,412 --> 00:22:52,705
I ordered yours. It's coming.

346
00:22:52,830 --> 00:22:53,956
Oh, thanks.

347
00:23:00,588 --> 00:23:03,591
Energy is an asset.
Let's stock up while we can.

348
00:23:03,716 --> 00:23:04,550
Yes.

349
00:23:04,675 --> 00:23:05,593
-Ms. Ma.
-Yes?

350
00:23:05,718 --> 00:23:06,844
RED GINSENG

351
00:23:06,969 --> 00:23:08,012
Oh, thank you.

352
00:23:08,930 --> 00:23:09,764
Here.

353
00:23:16,687 --> 00:23:17,897
Change my name.

354
00:23:18,731 --> 00:23:20,608
-No.
-Come on.

355
00:23:21,901 --> 00:23:23,027
Dad.

356
00:23:23,152 --> 00:23:26,030
I was too scared to ask you this before.

357
00:23:26,697 --> 00:23:28,741
Since my name, Sang-su,

358
00:23:29,325 --> 00:23:31,077
means a constant value
that never changes,

359
00:23:32,328 --> 00:23:35,123
does it signify "Lee Yeong-do
and Ko Mun-yeong's unchanging love"?

360
00:23:35,915 --> 00:23:36,874
It doesn't, does it?

361
00:23:36,999 --> 00:23:38,251
It does.

362
00:23:40,419 --> 00:23:41,921
I tried to stop them for your sake.

363
00:23:46,509 --> 00:23:47,885
I knew it!

364
00:23:48,010 --> 00:23:49,220
It's why I didn't ask.

365
00:23:49,846 --> 00:23:51,514
Just let me change my name!

366
00:23:51,639 --> 00:23:54,183
Hey, be quiet.
Aren't you embarrassed in front of him?

367
00:23:56,602 --> 00:23:59,147
No! Change my name! Please!

368
00:24:00,398 --> 00:24:01,524
Yellow forsythia…

369
00:24:03,109 --> 00:24:05,820
Was the name of the  hanbok  shop owner's
granddaughter Na-ri?

370
00:24:09,740 --> 00:24:12,785
Was the sink over there?

371
00:24:16,497 --> 00:24:17,456
Who's that?

372
00:24:22,837 --> 00:24:24,672
I'm the tallest in my class.

373
00:24:25,798 --> 00:24:27,675
You take after Namgung, huh?

374
00:24:27,800 --> 00:24:28,843
He was the tallest.

375
00:24:28,968 --> 00:24:30,595
I'm going to be taller.

376
00:24:33,639 --> 00:24:35,516
There are mosquitoes everywhere.

377
00:24:35,641 --> 00:24:37,643
I didn't want to come. I'm not eating.

378
00:24:37,768 --> 00:24:39,103
Yellow forsythia…

379
00:24:43,316 --> 00:24:44,233
Say "ah."

380
00:24:44,358 --> 00:24:45,234
Good boy.

381
00:24:45,359 --> 00:24:46,569
You look like Karina.

382
00:24:48,112 --> 00:24:49,280
He's really like Namgung.

383
00:24:49,947 --> 00:24:51,616
Hey, he just has a good eye.

384
00:24:52,241 --> 00:24:55,536
Grandma, can I come over
whenever I want  japchae ?

385
00:24:55,661 --> 00:24:58,331
Of course, whenever you want it.

386
00:24:59,582 --> 00:25:00,917
No.

387
00:25:02,168 --> 00:25:03,711
You're going to the shelter tomorrow.

388
00:25:03,836 --> 00:25:05,504
That's why we all came here.

389
00:25:07,757 --> 00:25:10,176
You'll never see these people again.

390
00:25:11,427 --> 00:25:12,428
This is it.

391
00:25:21,520 --> 00:25:22,355
BROTHER CLEANING

392
00:25:22,480 --> 00:25:23,731
Hey, man.

393
00:25:23,856 --> 00:25:25,566
Did you have to go that far?

394
00:25:27,652 --> 00:25:29,403
And why is it the last time?

395
00:25:29,528 --> 00:25:30,738
If he's at Pastor Kim's--

396
00:25:30,863 --> 00:25:32,281
I'll look into adoption abroad.

397
00:25:34,242 --> 00:25:36,577
If Hwa-young and Ju-wan waive custody,

398
00:25:37,203 --> 00:25:39,372
I'll be appointed as his legal guardian,

399
00:25:40,289 --> 00:25:41,749
then I'll send him abroad.

400
00:25:42,583 --> 00:25:43,501
Hey, Namgung.

401
00:25:43,626 --> 00:25:44,877
In Korea,

402
00:25:45,670 --> 00:25:47,421
even if the law forbids it,

403
00:25:48,547 --> 00:25:50,675
everything about blood ties
can be found in a week

404
00:25:50,800 --> 00:25:52,969
if you give a private investigator
two million won.

405
00:25:53,970 --> 00:25:56,681
Mi-do is already attached to him.

406
00:25:59,100 --> 00:26:00,142
She just pities him.

407
00:26:01,560 --> 00:26:04,438
Mi-do sees me in him.

408
00:26:04,563 --> 00:26:06,232
She just feels so sorry for him.

409
00:26:06,357 --> 00:26:09,151
Come on, what do you mean?
It's not like that.

410
00:26:09,277 --> 00:26:10,611
You know it, too.

411
00:26:12,154 --> 00:26:14,156
Mi-do sometimes says she pities me.

412
00:26:16,993 --> 00:26:18,995
I know Mi-do doesn't realize it.

413
00:26:21,455 --> 00:26:22,999
And she means nothing by it.

414
00:26:25,501 --> 00:26:27,211
But whenever Mi-do says that,

415
00:26:28,796 --> 00:26:31,299
my life feels so miserable and pathetic.

416
00:26:32,675 --> 00:26:34,719
I feel like I'm seven years old again.

417
00:26:44,895 --> 00:26:45,938
Sorry.

418
00:26:47,356 --> 00:26:48,357
He just made me…

419
00:26:51,444 --> 00:26:52,987
What are you talking about?

420
00:26:53,654 --> 00:26:55,072
I say those things to you?

421
00:26:56,282 --> 00:26:58,492
-Mi-do.
-No, I've never said those things.

422
00:26:59,618 --> 00:27:01,287
What am I, crazy?

423
00:27:01,412 --> 00:27:02,330
Don't lie.

424
00:27:04,081 --> 00:27:05,791
Actually, you do often.

425
00:27:05,916 --> 00:27:06,751
Hey.

426
00:27:09,754 --> 00:27:10,963
You do it often.

427
00:27:11,756 --> 00:27:13,424
You do it all the time around us.

428
00:27:25,770 --> 00:27:27,855
No, Mi-do. He's exaggerating it.

429
00:27:27,980 --> 00:27:29,940
Why did you never tell me?

430
00:27:30,066 --> 00:27:31,734
You should've told me.

431
00:27:32,401 --> 00:27:34,987
I knew you meant nothing by it,
so I was fine.

432
00:27:35,112 --> 00:27:37,031
How could you be fine with that?

433
00:27:37,156 --> 00:27:38,449
How?

434
00:27:45,039 --> 00:27:46,248
Namgung.

435
00:27:47,375 --> 00:27:49,543
I've never thought of you like that.

436
00:27:49,668 --> 00:27:52,046
I mean it, really.

437
00:27:52,171 --> 00:27:53,381
I know, Mi-do.

438
00:27:54,965 --> 00:27:57,009
You know I always speak without thinking.

439
00:27:57,760 --> 00:27:59,720
I have no filter.

440
00:27:59,845 --> 00:28:02,390
So I probably just said it
without really thinking.

441
00:28:03,140 --> 00:28:05,226
I swear I didn't mean it like that.

442
00:28:06,060 --> 00:28:07,228
I know, Mi-do.

443
00:28:08,187 --> 00:28:09,105
Stop it.

444
00:28:11,023 --> 00:28:12,149
Namgung.

445
00:28:13,150 --> 00:28:16,028
I just wanted to give you everything.

446
00:28:17,238 --> 00:28:20,741
I just wanted to give you
everything I had.

447
00:28:22,326 --> 00:28:23,285
I know.

448
00:28:24,328 --> 00:28:25,329
Thank you.

449
00:28:27,415 --> 00:28:30,418
When you thank me like that, I just…

450
00:28:31,377 --> 00:28:32,336
I…

451
00:28:40,469 --> 00:28:41,971
Namgung, I'm sorry.

452
00:28:43,806 --> 00:28:45,224
I'm so sorry.

453
00:28:46,600 --> 00:28:47,476
I really am.

454
00:28:59,780 --> 00:29:00,865
She quit?

455
00:29:00,990 --> 00:29:02,116
Yes.

456
00:29:02,241 --> 00:29:05,077
We went out of our way to hire
an older, inexperienced person.

457
00:29:05,202 --> 00:29:07,163
And she's been a no-show for three days.

458
00:29:07,288 --> 00:29:09,540
Wow, this is ridiculous.

459
00:29:12,084 --> 00:29:15,129
PLEASE ANSWER

460
00:29:15,254 --> 00:29:16,797
ATTORNEY HAN TAE-SEUNG

461
00:29:18,757 --> 00:29:20,009
It was you.

462
00:29:20,134 --> 00:29:22,720
If you hurt Mi-do any further,

463
00:29:24,096 --> 00:29:25,723
you're a dead man.

464
00:29:26,390 --> 00:29:29,852
How can you love the man
who caused your father's death?

465
00:29:40,446 --> 00:29:42,490
Sol has grown so much, hasn't he?

466
00:29:42,615 --> 00:29:43,741
-He really has.
-Yeah.

467
00:29:43,866 --> 00:29:45,951
Sol, do you remember the pastor?

468
00:29:46,076 --> 00:29:48,120
-No.
-You really don't remember?

469
00:29:48,245 --> 00:29:49,163
Say hello.

470
00:29:49,288 --> 00:29:50,539
Hello.

471
00:29:50,664 --> 00:29:52,416
-Hi, Sol.
-What a good boy.

472
00:29:52,541 --> 00:29:54,460
-Shall we go inside and talk?
-Come here.

473
00:29:55,044 --> 00:29:57,963
They have a lot of experience.
They'll take good care of him.

474
00:29:59,173 --> 00:30:01,300
-He's grown up so well.
-Right? He's grown so much.

475
00:30:01,425 --> 00:30:04,470
ANON TEMPORARY CHILD SHELTER

476
00:30:06,388 --> 00:30:07,556
Ho!

477
00:30:19,735 --> 00:30:21,695
I won't hate you.

478
00:30:22,947 --> 00:30:24,073
So please…

479
00:30:25,699 --> 00:30:27,201
So please…

480
00:30:28,452 --> 00:30:30,162
Please…

481
00:31:04,280 --> 00:31:07,741
Stay healthy, Sol.

482
00:31:10,995 --> 00:31:12,204
Ho!

483
00:31:13,414 --> 00:31:15,833
Ho!

484
00:31:16,500 --> 00:31:18,836
Ho!

485
00:31:34,685 --> 00:31:35,769
Is it…

486
00:31:37,146 --> 00:31:38,314
because of me?

487
00:31:39,690 --> 00:31:40,983
Is it because of me

488
00:31:41,108 --> 00:31:44,069
that you're not getting attached to Sol
and pushing him away?

489
00:31:46,238 --> 00:31:48,574
If you treat Sol
like Hwa-young treated you,

490
00:31:48,699 --> 00:31:50,034
we'll all suffer.

491
00:31:50,159 --> 00:31:51,994
-So--
-Mi-do, I…

492
00:31:54,788 --> 00:31:56,790
I absolutely hate him.

493
00:32:00,294 --> 00:32:02,004
He reminds me of Han Ju-wan.

494
00:32:05,132 --> 00:32:07,801
Looking at him
just reminds me of Han Ju-wan.

495
00:32:10,721 --> 00:32:12,598
And getting attached?

496
00:32:14,016 --> 00:32:15,142
Don't you remember?

497
00:32:16,769 --> 00:32:17,936
I already…

498
00:32:20,272 --> 00:32:22,024
abandoned him once.

499
00:32:23,817 --> 00:32:25,027
Did that woman come by…

500
00:32:35,454 --> 00:32:38,540
First, please fill out
this child abandonment report.

501
00:32:38,666 --> 00:32:42,211
Then, please sign the child transfer
agreement for facility placement,

502
00:32:42,336 --> 00:32:47,299
and the form confirming
you refuse to support him.

503
00:32:51,095 --> 00:32:53,430
THE ABANDONED CHILD
WILL BE PLACED IN PROTECTIVE CUSTODY

504
00:33:01,063 --> 00:33:03,857
CHILD CANNOT BE PLACED WITH FAMILY
ANON TEMPORARY CHILD SHELTER

505
00:33:13,575 --> 00:33:15,869
Mi-do, to me, my family is just

506
00:33:16,453 --> 00:33:18,080
you, Ms. Ma,

507
00:33:18,205 --> 00:33:20,040
Yeong-do,

508
00:33:21,375 --> 00:33:22,626
Wan-do,

509
00:33:24,002 --> 00:33:24,920
and Sang-su.

510
00:33:28,966 --> 00:33:30,426
There's no one else.

511
00:33:49,486 --> 00:33:51,071
Oh, give it here.

512
00:33:51,196 --> 00:33:53,073
You paid, so I'll carry it.

513
00:33:53,198 --> 00:33:55,868
Nonsense. Let's carry it together.

514
00:33:55,993 --> 00:33:57,870
Dad, are you crazy?

515
00:33:57,995 --> 00:34:00,038
That guy is married!

516
00:34:00,164 --> 00:34:01,123
THREE YEARS AGO

517
00:34:01,290 --> 00:34:03,542
Just live as you used to, Dad.

518
00:34:03,667 --> 00:34:06,462
When did you start being serious
about one person?

519
00:34:06,587 --> 00:34:08,672
You didn't last a year with Su-yeon's dad!

520
00:34:12,009 --> 00:34:13,385
I looked into it.

521
00:34:14,386 --> 00:34:17,389
This guy hasn't even
divorced his wife yet,

522
00:34:17,514 --> 00:34:19,099
and he doesn't plan to.

523
00:34:19,224 --> 00:34:22,269
He only approached you for your money.

524
00:34:23,228 --> 00:34:25,105
If you keep seeing him,

525
00:34:26,064 --> 00:34:27,024
I'll post it online.

526
00:34:34,615 --> 00:34:35,908
Don't you dare.

527
00:34:37,785 --> 00:34:38,952
I mean it.

528
00:34:39,077 --> 00:34:41,622
Post it again, and you'll regret it.

529
00:34:43,248 --> 00:34:45,042
-Dad…
-Please, just stop…

530
00:34:47,795 --> 00:34:48,921
Stop saying that.

531
00:34:58,430 --> 00:35:00,307
I just want to stop…

532
00:35:02,768 --> 00:35:03,977
being your dad.

533
00:36:17,009 --> 00:36:18,176
Sorry, it's so early.

534
00:36:33,859 --> 00:36:36,945
See? I told you he's a light sleeper
and would wake up, Mom.

535
00:36:37,946 --> 00:36:40,616
Mom insisted on making you breakfast.

536
00:36:40,741 --> 00:36:42,993
You wouldn't have come if I asked,
would you?

537
00:36:44,119 --> 00:36:46,663
Dad, you promised me
two hours at the internet café.

538
00:36:47,998 --> 00:36:48,957
I tried to stop them.

539
00:36:50,417 --> 00:36:51,627
Come on, now.

540
00:36:52,711 --> 00:36:53,545
Oh.

541
00:36:59,301 --> 00:37:00,510
Hold on.

542
00:37:01,595 --> 00:37:02,596
Uncle Ho.

543
00:37:03,263 --> 00:37:04,097
Here.

544
00:37:07,309 --> 00:37:08,727
Sol wanted to get you

545
00:37:09,436 --> 00:37:11,897
a gift or something,

546
00:37:12,022 --> 00:37:14,650
so he asked me what you like.

547
00:37:14,775 --> 00:37:16,193
So I told him.

548
00:37:17,110 --> 00:37:19,821
I think I gave him
some pretty good advice.

549
00:37:23,325 --> 00:37:24,242
Come on, hurry.

550
00:37:24,826 --> 00:37:25,786
Oh.

551
00:37:25,911 --> 00:37:27,537
How is it?

552
00:37:29,247 --> 00:37:30,874
-Try this, Yeong-do.
-Why? Is it salty?

553
00:37:31,875 --> 00:37:32,751
How is it?

554
00:37:32,876 --> 00:37:35,087
Did you make this? Why is it so salty?

555
00:37:35,212 --> 00:37:36,296
-Mom made it.
-Did I?

556
00:37:36,421 --> 00:37:37,589
Hey, give it here.

557
00:37:37,714 --> 00:37:39,341
Mom, it's fine. Try it.

558
00:37:39,466 --> 00:37:41,134
She hasn't cooked in a while.

559
00:37:43,887 --> 00:37:44,888
It's delicious.

560
00:37:45,013 --> 00:37:46,807
-See? It's good.
-Yes, it's good.

561
00:37:46,932 --> 00:37:48,392
It's… really good.

562
00:37:56,608 --> 00:37:57,484
Sol.

563
00:38:08,412 --> 00:38:09,746
Grab your jacket.

564
00:38:36,815 --> 00:38:37,941
Darn it.

565
00:39:20,275 --> 00:39:21,151
Don't touch.

566
00:39:24,738 --> 00:39:25,822
Just look at them.

567
00:39:34,081 --> 00:39:34,915
Your name…

568
00:39:38,251 --> 00:39:39,544
I'm who gave it to you.

569
00:39:41,338 --> 00:39:42,422
Say, "Brother."

570
00:39:42,547 --> 00:39:44,299
Brother.

571
00:39:47,260 --> 00:39:48,470
What are you going to do?

572
00:39:49,679 --> 00:39:51,681
I thought he was a big catch,

573
00:39:51,807 --> 00:39:54,309
but he turned out to be a total scumbag.

574
00:39:56,186 --> 00:39:59,272
I was just blinded by greed
and made a bad bet.

575
00:40:03,568 --> 00:40:06,571
First, I need to tie him down legally.

576
00:40:06,696 --> 00:40:09,741
I'll squeeze every last penny out of him.

577
00:40:10,450 --> 00:40:11,576
His mom's side has money.

578
00:40:11,701 --> 00:40:13,370
Mom! Seriously…

579
00:40:19,000 --> 00:40:20,794
Just pick something, okay?

580
00:40:29,136 --> 00:40:31,513
BIRTH REGISTRATION FORM

581
00:40:35,809 --> 00:40:38,270
It's not "Sol" from the musical scale.

582
00:40:39,521 --> 00:40:40,897
It means "pine tree."

583
00:40:41,022 --> 00:40:41,940
NAME: HAN SOL

584
00:40:42,065 --> 00:40:44,651
I chose that so you'd grow up strong.

585
00:40:47,112 --> 00:40:48,238
Do you like it?

586
00:40:49,614 --> 00:40:51,658
Well, it's not bad.

587
00:40:56,872 --> 00:40:57,706
Sol.

588
00:40:59,791 --> 00:41:03,461
A lot of people
are going to pity you in the future.

589
00:41:04,921 --> 00:41:06,840
And because they pity you,

590
00:41:07,883 --> 00:41:09,301
they're going to love you.

591
00:41:10,677 --> 00:41:12,596
-The  japchae  is good.
-Want some more?

592
00:41:12,721 --> 00:41:13,889
-I'm fine.
-It's good.

593
00:41:14,014 --> 00:41:15,265
-I'm good.
-Me too.

594
00:41:15,390 --> 00:41:17,225
Here, try some of this, okay?

595
00:41:18,685 --> 00:41:23,190
So there will be many times
when you feel miserable and pathetic.

596
00:41:24,858 --> 00:41:25,984
But Sol,

597
00:41:26,693 --> 00:41:28,486
even love given out of pity…

598
00:41:29,654 --> 00:41:31,406
is truly a warm feeling.

599
00:41:32,115 --> 00:41:33,617
It's not fake. It's real.

600
00:41:34,492 --> 00:41:36,453
It's genuine love for you.

601
00:41:52,219 --> 00:41:53,386
So,

602
00:41:55,222 --> 00:41:57,682
just because
you feel miserable or pathetic,

603
00:42:00,185 --> 00:42:03,188
don't doubt that love or push it away.

604
00:42:07,108 --> 00:42:09,194
You have to know its worth

605
00:42:10,320 --> 00:42:11,488
and be thankful.

606
00:42:12,447 --> 00:42:14,282
Learn to love others in return.

607
00:42:16,868 --> 00:42:18,119
That's the way to live.

608
00:42:23,625 --> 00:42:25,669
Did you have a snack earlier?

609
00:42:25,794 --> 00:42:28,588
Above all, even if others pity you,

610
00:42:29,714 --> 00:42:31,383
- you…
-I had a late-night snack.

611
00:42:31,508 --> 00:42:32,759
-Did you?
-… must never

612
00:42:33,426 --> 00:42:35,387
pity yourself.

613
00:42:36,012 --> 00:42:36,846
Chicken feet.

614
00:42:36,972 --> 00:42:38,181
They're so good, right?

615
00:42:38,306 --> 00:42:41,726
You need to be someone who loves

616
00:42:42,352 --> 00:42:44,312
and cherishes yourself the most.

617
00:42:45,689 --> 00:42:48,233
Only then can you love others,

618
00:42:49,150 --> 00:42:51,486
and accept the love they give you.

619
00:42:55,198 --> 00:42:56,449
So, Sol,

620
00:42:57,325 --> 00:42:58,201
make sure

621
00:42:59,536 --> 00:43:01,454
you grow up loving yourself.

622
00:43:18,138 --> 00:43:20,724
This jerk picked a fight with me first!

623
00:43:21,474 --> 00:43:22,309
Detective.

624
00:43:22,434 --> 00:43:24,352
He's obviously a drug addict

625
00:43:24,477 --> 00:43:26,688
or an escapee from a mental ward!

626
00:43:26,813 --> 00:43:28,315
I hit my head really hard

627
00:43:28,440 --> 00:43:30,775
on the asphalt… Ouch.

628
00:43:30,900 --> 00:43:32,944
Damn it, my head, ouch…

629
00:43:35,280 --> 00:43:36,114
Mr. Han Tae-seung.

630
00:43:36,239 --> 00:43:39,034
You were sent home last time
for a psychiatric evaluation,

631
00:43:39,159 --> 00:43:40,618
but not this time.

632
00:43:40,744 --> 00:43:43,621
There were no security cameras,
but we have witnesses.

633
00:43:43,747 --> 00:43:44,956
Call your guardian.

634
00:43:45,081 --> 00:43:46,875
He really is a psycho.

635
00:43:47,000 --> 00:43:48,918
Sir, lock him up right now!

636
00:43:49,044 --> 00:43:51,129
I get it, so calm down and sit.

637
00:43:51,880 --> 00:43:52,881
Jeez…

638
00:43:53,006 --> 00:43:55,342
Ouch, my head…

639
00:43:58,970 --> 00:43:59,971
It was you, right?

640
00:44:00,096 --> 00:44:02,098
You requested the warehouse audit,
didn't you?

641
00:44:04,809 --> 00:44:06,686
I just followed the manual.

642
00:44:07,562 --> 00:44:10,190
Unauthorized disposal is subject to audit.

643
00:44:10,315 --> 00:44:13,193
You know exactly why I tossed it, punk.

644
00:44:17,030 --> 00:44:20,325
You may hate all the cheap ingredients,

645
00:44:21,076 --> 00:44:23,870
but they're safe
and approved by the MFDS.

646
00:44:24,621 --> 00:44:26,915
You can't just toss them on your own.

647
00:44:27,040 --> 00:44:28,583
Damn it!

648
00:44:28,708 --> 00:44:30,085
-Hey!
-Manager Eom!

649
00:44:30,210 --> 00:44:31,878
-Stop him, Manager Jeong.
-Manager Eom.

650
00:44:32,003 --> 00:44:33,254
Please let go of him…

651
00:44:35,465 --> 00:44:36,841
All right, I'll let you continue.

652
00:44:37,592 --> 00:44:41,096
How could you do this to me?

653
00:44:41,221 --> 00:44:42,263
Huh?

654
00:44:55,610 --> 00:44:58,154
The fall launch is definitely dead.

655
00:44:58,988 --> 00:45:01,157
And if you get disciplined…

656
00:45:03,076 --> 00:45:05,829
He thinks he's with the brass now, huh?

657
00:45:06,955 --> 00:45:08,706
After everything I did for him.

658
00:45:13,670 --> 00:45:15,505
-Oh no, I'm sorry!
-Hey, careful…

659
00:45:15,630 --> 00:45:16,923
It's fine.

660
00:45:17,048 --> 00:45:18,633
I'll just go to the restroom.

661
00:45:18,758 --> 00:45:20,427
Please go ahead.

662
00:45:24,431 --> 00:45:27,183
Eight whole years together,

663
00:45:27,308 --> 00:45:29,561
and he backstabs me in just three months?

664
00:45:30,937 --> 00:45:32,397
It's obvious, sir.

665
00:45:33,106 --> 00:45:33,982
Oh, is it?

666
00:45:34,941 --> 00:45:36,526
Wait, what is?

667
00:45:36,651 --> 00:45:39,112
I know you and Assistant Manager Namgung
are staging it.

668
00:45:39,237 --> 00:45:40,321
You can stop acting.

669
00:45:40,447 --> 00:45:42,198
What are you talking about?

670
00:45:42,323 --> 00:45:43,616
You saw us earlier.

671
00:45:43,741 --> 00:45:45,201
I grabbed him and shook him--

672
00:45:45,326 --> 00:45:46,870
Facing a disciplinary hearing

673
00:45:46,995 --> 00:45:49,038
and at least a pay cut,

674
00:45:49,914 --> 00:45:52,041
yet buying pork ribs
for 15,900 won per person?

675
00:45:52,167 --> 00:45:53,835
It doesn't make sense.

676
00:45:53,960 --> 00:45:57,005
Well, times like this call

677
00:45:57,547 --> 00:45:58,798
for treating you guys well--

678
00:46:00,216 --> 00:46:02,469
Then why did you buy
cheap, 7,900-won pork skin

679
00:46:02,594 --> 00:46:05,013
when the fifth sample fell through?

680
00:46:06,014 --> 00:46:07,724
Well, that was…

681
00:46:10,768 --> 00:46:12,729
If you don't tell me your plan,

682
00:46:12,854 --> 00:46:14,272
I'll tell Mr. Baek, too.

683
00:46:17,025 --> 00:46:18,568
Were you always like this?

684
00:46:19,694 --> 00:46:21,154
Anyway, never mind that.

685
00:46:22,113 --> 00:46:23,448
How much do you know?

686
00:46:57,106 --> 00:46:59,567
Forget what that detective said earlier.

687
00:46:59,692 --> 00:47:02,612
I usually black out when I drink,
and I drank too much.

688
00:47:04,405 --> 00:47:06,658
It's true. You don't buy it?

689
00:47:06,783 --> 00:47:07,992
You think it's an act?

690
00:47:08,117 --> 00:47:10,328
Well, you're right.

691
00:47:12,372 --> 00:47:14,999
You ignored my calls.
What else could I do?

692
00:47:15,124 --> 00:47:17,085
I had to rely on the authorities.

693
00:47:17,877 --> 00:47:19,504
This is all your fault.

694
00:47:23,633 --> 00:47:25,385
Is your rage meter still at level five?

695
00:47:25,510 --> 00:47:26,761
Or level six?

696
00:47:32,016 --> 00:47:33,184
I'm sorry.

697
00:47:33,309 --> 00:47:34,936
I went too far that day.

698
00:47:36,437 --> 00:47:37,397
Attorney Han?

699
00:47:46,781 --> 00:47:48,199
Are you here for a case?

700
00:47:48,866 --> 00:47:51,286
I was worried when you left Jaekang.

701
00:47:51,411 --> 00:47:53,037
Guess people still hire you.

702
00:47:53,162 --> 00:47:54,956
Heard you did well with Hanbuk's case.

703
00:47:55,873 --> 00:47:57,125
Congrats.

704
00:47:57,250 --> 00:47:59,002
Stop disgracing our profession.

705
00:48:01,546 --> 00:48:03,047
Drinking parties, lobbying…

706
00:48:03,172 --> 00:48:05,466
Stop surviving on things like that.

707
00:48:06,467 --> 00:48:07,427
Honestly,

708
00:48:07,969 --> 00:48:10,263
you made me ashamed to be a lawyer.

709
00:48:13,933 --> 00:48:15,184
Ashamed?

710
00:48:17,478 --> 00:48:19,439
You should be ashamed of losing.

711
00:48:20,356 --> 00:48:22,567
Unlike you, my parents
aren't judges or prosecutors.

712
00:48:22,692 --> 00:48:24,861
I have to do whatever it takes to win.

713
00:48:30,033 --> 00:48:31,200
Keep up the good work.

714
00:48:32,535 --> 00:48:34,537
Well, you've even killed someone.

715
00:48:34,662 --> 00:48:36,289
Acting like a jerk must be easy.

716
00:48:40,084 --> 00:48:42,128
I'll sexually harass you in one minute.

717
00:48:43,463 --> 00:48:45,632
If you don't get lost right now,

718
00:48:45,757 --> 00:48:47,925
I'll pull your pants down and shame you.

719
00:48:48,051 --> 00:48:49,344
If I come at you,

720
00:48:49,469 --> 00:48:52,055
stripping you to your underwear
would be too easy.

721
00:48:53,097 --> 00:48:55,058
I mean it. I'm strong.

722
00:48:55,183 --> 00:48:57,101
What's this crazy woman saying?

723
00:48:57,852 --> 00:48:59,145
Twenty seconds left.

724
00:48:59,979 --> 00:49:02,273
Birds of a feather, seriously.

725
00:49:15,328 --> 00:49:17,538
All right, let's go! Round four!

726
00:49:17,664 --> 00:49:19,248
-This is great!
-Round four!

727
00:49:19,374 --> 00:49:20,208
Let's go!

728
00:49:23,002 --> 00:49:24,629
Assistant Manager Gung, nice!

729
00:49:24,754 --> 00:49:25,755
Thank you!

730
00:49:26,339 --> 00:49:27,173
Jeong Yeon-ho, great!

731
00:49:27,298 --> 00:49:29,759
-See you tomorrow.
-See you.

732
00:49:31,719 --> 00:49:33,096
Hey, bro.

733
00:49:33,221 --> 00:49:35,640
Just have one more drink with me, okay?

734
00:49:36,182 --> 00:49:39,602
I have so much
I want to talk to you about.

735
00:49:39,727 --> 00:49:40,895
Sir.

736
00:49:41,020 --> 00:49:45,108
I booked that lounge club
you said you wanted to go to.

737
00:49:45,233 --> 00:49:46,275
A club?

738
00:49:46,401 --> 00:49:48,319
Yes, so let's just go home tonight.

739
00:49:48,444 --> 00:49:49,320
Huh?

740
00:49:49,445 --> 00:49:51,155
-And next week…
-Next week?

741
00:49:51,280 --> 00:49:52,365
…let's go there!

742
00:49:52,490 --> 00:49:54,534
Let's go there next week!

743
00:49:54,659 --> 00:49:56,494
-All right.
-Let's go!

744
00:49:56,619 --> 00:49:58,079
-Let's go!
-In you go.

745
00:49:59,539 --> 00:50:01,499
Bye! Let's go!

746
00:50:01,624 --> 00:50:03,501
Next week!

747
00:51:09,233 --> 00:51:10,318
Sol.

748
00:51:14,614 --> 00:51:16,365
I don't hate you.

749
00:51:19,827 --> 00:51:21,579
I actually care about you a lot.

750
00:51:25,333 --> 00:51:28,169
Way more than you think.

751
00:51:30,546 --> 00:51:31,714
But Sol,

752
00:51:33,049 --> 00:51:34,550
I care about myself more.

753
00:51:35,927 --> 00:51:37,094
I'm going to try.

754
00:51:38,012 --> 00:51:39,680
I'm going to try loving myself more.

755
00:51:42,016 --> 00:51:44,560
That's why I decided not to stay with you.

756
00:51:46,813 --> 00:51:48,105
So I'm not

757
00:51:49,232 --> 00:51:51,400
going to feel sorry for you.

758
00:51:51,526 --> 00:51:53,778
I'll always love you

759
00:51:54,946 --> 00:51:56,656
and care for you a lot.

760
00:51:58,658 --> 00:51:59,909
So, Sol.

761
00:52:03,371 --> 00:52:04,831
Could you please…

762
00:52:07,750 --> 00:52:11,671
not hate me too much
and love me, too?

763
00:52:39,282 --> 00:52:40,491
Assistant Manager Namgung.

764
00:52:42,827 --> 00:52:43,703
Hey.

765
00:52:44,745 --> 00:52:46,163
It's Park Su-a.

766
00:52:47,707 --> 00:52:49,959
You're crazy. How much did you drink?

767
00:52:51,836 --> 00:52:53,880
Stay here. I'll go buy some water.

768
00:52:54,005 --> 00:52:55,548
Park Su-a.

769
00:53:01,554 --> 00:53:04,265
You know, last time…

770
00:53:06,767 --> 00:53:08,936
What you told me

771
00:53:09,687 --> 00:53:12,940
when I said my dream
was to be a general manager.

772
00:53:13,900 --> 00:53:15,902
What you said at the convenience store.

773
00:53:17,528 --> 00:53:18,821
Huh?

774
00:53:18,946 --> 00:53:20,573
That I used to be an outcast?

775
00:53:20,698 --> 00:53:22,033
No.

776
00:53:22,158 --> 00:53:24,243
Oh, that life isn't like dramas?

777
00:53:24,368 --> 00:53:26,329
No, that's what I told you.

778
00:53:29,332 --> 00:53:30,875
That I'm highly resilient, right?

779
00:53:31,000 --> 00:53:32,960
No!

780
00:53:33,628 --> 00:53:35,504
Not that.

781
00:53:40,635 --> 00:53:42,678
When I said your dream was cool?

782
00:53:43,387 --> 00:53:44,388
Yes.

783
00:53:46,891 --> 00:53:47,850
That.

784
00:53:51,979 --> 00:53:54,607
Can you tell me that one more time?

785
00:54:04,659 --> 00:54:05,743
You're cool.

786
00:54:09,664 --> 00:54:12,041
You're really, really cool.

787
00:54:37,608 --> 00:54:38,901
What are you doing?

788
00:54:41,445 --> 00:54:43,114
I'm not looking. Go ahead and cry.

789
00:54:45,449 --> 00:54:48,577
Isn't the girlfriend supposed
to wipe my tears right now?

790
00:54:49,829 --> 00:54:51,497
Then you won't be able to cry.

791
00:54:57,253 --> 00:54:58,713
Then just leave.

792
00:54:59,547 --> 00:55:00,423
No…

793
00:55:01,465 --> 00:55:02,591
I'll stay with you.

794
00:55:03,718 --> 00:55:05,052
So…

795
00:55:05,845 --> 00:55:08,806
tell me when you're done crying.

796
00:55:39,587 --> 00:55:41,005
You're so silly.

797
00:56:05,362 --> 00:56:07,073
I'm sorry. I was wrong.

798
00:56:10,451 --> 00:56:11,577
I never should've…

799
00:56:13,162 --> 00:56:14,705
said those things.

800
00:56:16,624 --> 00:56:17,833
It's just that

801
00:56:18,626 --> 00:56:20,336
I like you so much,

802
00:56:22,505 --> 00:56:24,632
and I was so jealous of Namgung Ho.

803
00:56:31,514 --> 00:56:33,182
Are you going to keep ignoring me?

804
00:56:46,862 --> 00:56:47,988
Mi-do.

805
00:56:50,574 --> 00:56:52,535
Are you really going to shut me out?

806
00:57:06,590 --> 00:57:08,759
I can't leave Namgung.

807
00:57:12,805 --> 00:57:13,889
You know…

808
00:57:16,725 --> 00:57:17,810
That day…

809
00:57:23,566 --> 00:57:25,359
The person responsible for my dad's death…

810
00:57:29,655 --> 00:57:31,073
wasn't Namgung.

811
00:57:38,122 --> 00:57:39,165
It was me.

812
00:57:44,879 --> 00:57:47,006
My dad died because of me.

813
00:57:54,555 --> 00:57:55,806
Someone fell in the water!

814
00:57:56,473 --> 00:57:58,309
Hurry, help!

815
00:58:03,147 --> 00:58:04,565
-Dad!
-Yes?

816
00:58:04,690 --> 00:58:07,651
Dad, hurry, save him! What are you doing?

817
00:58:08,319 --> 00:58:12,198
If something happens to him,
I'll be so sad.

818
00:58:12,948 --> 00:58:14,366
If he dies,

819
00:58:14,491 --> 00:58:17,703
it's going to break my heart.

820
00:58:18,370 --> 00:58:20,581
You told me to speak my mind!

821
00:58:20,706 --> 00:58:24,418
Dad, hurry and save him! Now!

822
00:58:24,543 --> 00:58:27,046
Hurry up and save him!

823
00:58:27,171 --> 00:58:29,381
Dad!

824
00:58:29,506 --> 00:58:31,133
Dad!

825
00:58:31,258 --> 00:58:33,052
Okay, I will.

826
00:58:34,553 --> 00:58:37,139
I'll go save him and come back, okay?

827
00:58:38,515 --> 00:58:39,391
Okay.

828
00:58:40,226 --> 00:58:41,060
Hurry!

829
00:58:41,727 --> 00:58:42,853
I'll be back.

830
00:58:56,242 --> 00:58:57,451
It's all your fault.

831
00:58:58,160 --> 00:59:00,621
My husband died because of you.

832
00:59:01,330 --> 00:59:03,415
My kids' dad is dead because of you.

833
00:59:04,416 --> 00:59:06,126
Because of a thing like you.

834
00:59:07,169 --> 00:59:09,838
Because of someone like you!

835
00:59:10,422 --> 00:59:13,217
Why did my kids' dad have to die?

836
00:59:14,093 --> 00:59:15,135
Why?

837
00:59:15,928 --> 00:59:19,181
Why?

838
00:59:26,146 --> 00:59:30,526
Why?

839
00:59:40,327 --> 00:59:41,662
Namgung doesn't know.

840
00:59:42,663 --> 00:59:43,872
Nobody knows.

841
00:59:44,456 --> 00:59:46,709
I thought everyone would hate me.

842
00:59:48,752 --> 00:59:50,879
I hid behind Namgung like a coward.

843
00:59:55,801 --> 00:59:57,636
I can't leave Namgung.

844
01:00:02,182 --> 01:00:04,351
I have to be there for Namgung.

845
01:00:10,232 --> 01:00:11,358
I'm sorry.

846
01:00:13,027 --> 01:00:14,361
I was wrong.

847
01:00:15,821 --> 01:00:17,156
Apologizing won't work.

848
01:00:18,991 --> 01:00:20,701
I can't be with you.

849
01:00:21,327 --> 01:00:22,786
That's not it.

850
01:00:23,537 --> 01:00:25,164
That's not it…

851
01:00:32,671 --> 01:00:34,590
It must have been so hard.

852
01:00:37,426 --> 01:00:41,680
It must have been really, really hard.

853
01:00:43,349 --> 01:00:44,600
I…

854
01:00:45,225 --> 01:00:47,519
I had no idea…

855
01:00:48,896 --> 01:00:50,022
I'm just…

856
01:00:50,147 --> 01:00:52,733
I'm so sorry…

857
01:00:52,858 --> 01:00:53,776
I'm sorry.

858
01:01:26,892 --> 01:01:28,602
Hey, you startled me.

859
01:01:35,901 --> 01:01:36,902
What's wrong?

860
01:01:38,821 --> 01:01:40,197
Why do you look…

861
01:02:43,051 --> 01:02:44,887
THANK YOU TO CHOI HEEJIN
FOR HER SPECIAL APPEARANCE

862
01:02:45,512 --> 01:02:47,514
You wanted to get hurt. How does it feel?

863
01:02:48,390 --> 01:02:51,518
You like Park Su-a, don't you?

864
01:02:51,643 --> 01:02:54,271
You live like this all for Ms. Lee, right?

865
01:02:54,396 --> 01:02:56,773
Yes. To me, Lee Mi-do is everything.

866
01:02:56,899 --> 01:02:58,442
Are you disappointed?

867
01:02:58,567 --> 01:03:01,487
Oh, no. I think I really like you.

868
01:03:01,612 --> 01:03:03,447
We'll break up in about ten days.

869
01:03:03,572 --> 01:03:04,781
Will you sleep with me?

870
01:03:04,907 --> 01:03:06,158
Stop liking her.

871
01:03:07,659 --> 01:03:10,370
Stop liking her.

872
01:03:12,998 --> 01:03:14,958
Subtitle translation by Cayle Kim
